Phase 4.2 — settings screen: persisted settings replacing env-only configuration
========================================================================
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 4 item 2 ("settings screen: providers,
models, base URLs, max turns, execution mode with presets for OpenAI,
Anthropic and OpenAI-compatible endpoints")
Revision: the Phase 4.2 commit on main (after 6cc8f12)
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: ALL configuration was environment
variables read once at boot — defect §2 item 6 of the 2026-09-06 audit,
deferred to Phase 4; no settings surface, no persistence, no presets)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- event-store: migration v7 adds `app_settings` (single JSON document,
  docs/31 § Runtime configuration tables) + `settings.rs`
  (get/set/merge). Secrets NEVER live here: API keys belong to the
  secret broker (keychain broker = Phase 4 item 3, next).
- proto 17 → 19 requests: `GetSettingsRequest`,
  `UpdateSettingsCommand` (PARTIAL update — empty fields keep stored
  values), `SettingsView`; SurfaceResponse gains `settings`. TS
  bindings regenerated. Provider allowlist (openai | anthropic |
  openai-compatible), URL shape check, maxTurns 1..200,
  executionMode enum — enforced at the bridge schema guard BEFORE the
  privileged host sees the message (REQ ledger EV-0103 discipline).
- scheduler: PER-RUN overlay — each run takes provider / model /
  base_url / max_turns from the PERSISTED settings over the boot
  configuration (env stays the fallback for unset fields). A task
  started after a settings change runs with the new values with no
  daemon restart.
- execution_mode is a REAL consumer, not a stored string:
  "readonly" drops every write/external grant at the capability
  kernel — change.apply/shell.run/test.run are refused for the whole
  task; "default" keeps the full grant set. (Approval modes expand in
  Phase 5 per the work order.)
- desktop: a Settings screen (fleet ⇄ settings nav) with provider
  presets — OpenAI (api.openai.com/v1), Anthropic (api.anthropic.com),
  OpenAI-compatible with endpoint presets for Ollama (localhost:11434/
  v1), vLLM (localhost:8000/v1) and z.ai (api.z.ai/api/paas/v4) — plus
  model id, max turns, execution mode. Values load from GetSettings
  and save as partial UpdateSettings. An explicit note states API keys
  are NOT stored here (secret broker owns them).

PROOFS (full workspace suite exit 0, 503 Rust tests; desktop vitest 36
green; tsc clean; clippy clean)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
settings_e2e (REAL daemon + REAL model endpoint):
  persisted_settings_drive_runs_and_the_readonly_mode_refuses_edits . ok
  - UpdateSettings persists; GetSettings round-trips; both survive a
    core restart on the same DB (durable, docs/31)
  - the core booted with NO MODBIT_BASE_URL / MODBIT_MODEL /
    MODBIT_PROVIDER: the run REACHED the model endpoint configured in
    the settings (the fixture served the turns) — the overlay really
    routes
  - execution_mode=readonly: the model's change.apply attempt is
    refused by the kernel (denial rides the durable conversation) and
    the worktree file is byte-identical afterwards — nothing written
  default_mode_applies_the_edit ................................ ok
  - control: the SAME edit with execution_mode=default applies — the
    refusal is the SETTING's effect, not a breakage
- one debug iteration recorded: the fixture's turn index was used
  after increment (off-by-one served the finish text first); test
  fixed, production code untouched.

MUTATION CHECK (docs/55), against the Phase 4.2 commit:
  Mutation: the settings overlay disabled (boot config forced for every
  run, execution_mode forced default) -> the readonly E2E FAILED: with
  no overlay the run cannot reach the settings' model endpoint (no
  MODBIT_BASE_URL in the environment) and the task never completes.
  The overlay is load-bearing. REVERTED; post-revert green.

